Fixed an Interface whose only IP Addresses are IPv6 ending the Nautobot adapter's load with a `ValueError`, which took the whole job with it. The mask was reported by converting the prefix length to a dotted netmask, which is undefined above 32; addresses sort by IP version, so a dual-stack Interface put IPv4 first and was unaffected while an IPv6-only one raised. The prefix length is now what the sync records, which serves either version.
